      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1881 the Denver and Rio Grande Railroad reached Barranca, a station ten miles from the springs, boosting therapeutic visitors.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/ojo_caliente_hot_springs",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The resort’s 1860s Co‑ed Bathhouse, Historic Hotel, and 1924 Adobe Round Barn are all listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/ojo_caliente_hot_springs",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Established in 1868, Ojo Caliente Hot Springs ranks among the oldest health spas in the United States, blending indigenous and colonial healing traditions.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/ojo_caliente_hot_springs",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
